+# 137 · A window start aligned by a mask on power-of-two windows and by the remainder elsewhere proved equal
+
+[← All examples](../README.md)
+
+| Verdict | Categories | Severity if shipped | Change | Verified unit | Approach |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **⚠ Unverifiable** | functional, no-false-positive | none | refactor, behaviour change not intended | [`Window#counted`](../../examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java) | [B9: Regression verification](../../lib/README.md) |
+
+> The same rewrite of Crosscut's `Window` counter done right: a window that is a power of two aligns its start by clearing the reading's low bits, `nowNanos & -windowNanos`, the fast path for the filter's default windows, and any other window by the remainder as before. The regression proof shows the counter unchanged on every counter, reading and window: the tool's own checker in 0.5 s, the division left to the solver under the facts of every division, among them that a power of two divides by masking; JBMC did not finish the same harness within a minute.
+
+Tags: [resilience](../README.md#tag-resilience), [clocks-and-time](../README.md#tag-clocks-and-time), [rounding](../README.md#tag-rounding), [record-components](../README.md#tag-record-components), [own-checker](../README.md#tag-own-checker)
+
+## The change
+
+Compute the window's start as `nowNanos & -windowNanos` when `windowNanos` is a power of two (`(windowNanos & (windowNanos - 1)) == 0`) and as `nowNanos - nowNanos % windowNanos` otherwise. The tests are unchanged.
+
+**Before** ([`Window.java`](../../examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java), line 26):
+
+```java
+        if (windowNanos <= 0 || nowNanos < startNanos) {
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("the window must be positive and time must not go back");
+        }
+        long start = nowNanos - nowNanos % windowNanos;
+        return start == startNanos ? new Window(startNanos, count + 1) : new Window(start, 1);
+    }
+}
+```
+
+**After:**
+
+```java
+        if (windowNanos <= 0 || nowNanos < startNanos) {
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("the window must be positive and time must not go back");
+        }
+        // A window that is a power of two, the filter's default, aligns the start by clearing the low bits; any other
+        // by the remainder.
+        long start = (windowNanos & (windowNanos - 1)) == 0 ? nowNanos & -windowNanos : nowNanos - nowNanos % windowNanos;
+        return start == startNanos ? new Window(startNanos, count + 1) : new Window(start, 1);
+    }
+}
+```
+
